{
  "_comment": [
    ".claude/settings.json — the per-repository settings Claude Code reads.",
    "  cp templates/claude/settings.json.example .claude/settings.json",
    "  cp templates/claude/hooks/outbound_guard.sh .claude/hooks/",
    "  cp templates/hooks/outbound_permit.py     .claude/hooks/",
    "  chmod +x .claude/hooks/outbound_guard.sh .claude/hooks/outbound_permit.py",
    "",
    "This is the Claude Code half of the pair whose Codex half is",
    "templates/codex/config.toml.example. The two files configure the SAME",
    "three things — a date stamp on every turn, where memory is kept, and the",
    "brake on outward sends — because those are the places where a CLI's own",
    "defaults quietly change what your agent believes or is able to do.",
    "Everything else about this kit is CLI-agnostic on purpose (see AGENTS.md).",
    "",
    "JSON has no comments, so this key is the comment. Claude Code ignores",
    "unknown keys; leaving it in place costs nothing.",
    "",
    "hooks.UserPromptSubmit: the command's stdout is prepended to your turn,",
    "verbatim. Codex fires the same event but parses stdout as JSON, so its",
    "half of this pair wraps the same date in an envelope. See the note in",
    "templates/codex/config.toml.example before copying one command to the other.",
    "An agent that guesses today's date writes a deadline on the wrong weekday,",
    "and a wrong '(Mon)' does not look wrong on re-reading — the only way to",
    "catch it is to compare against a clock outside the model. So state it.",
    "",
    "hooks.PreToolUse: the outward brake. The instructions file says 'outward =",
    "ask first'; that sentence is a request, and a request is not a control.",
    "The hook is the control — it runs before every connector call and denies",
    "the outward ones, answering 'queue it in approval_queue.md' instead. Read",
    "templates/claude/hooks/outbound_guard.sh for what it stops and why, and",
    "docs/outbound-permits.md for how one approved message is let through.",
    "",
    "  · matcher 'mcp__.*' is a REGULAR EXPRESSION, and the '.*' is load-",
    "    bearing. A matcher of only letters, digits, _, -, spaces, ',' and '|'",
    "    is compared as an exact string — so a bare 'mcp__' would match no tool",
    "    at all, and the hook would never run. It would also never say so.",
    "  · ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} is exported to the hook process and expands to",
    "    the project root. Use it rather than a relative path: a relative path",
    "    resolves against the directory the CLI was STARTED in, which under",
    "    cron is your home directory, and a hook that cannot be executed is a",
    "    hook that silently is not there.",
    "  · THE HOST FAILS OPEN. A missing or unexecutable hook lets the call",
    "    proceed with a non-blocking notice; unparseable stdout does the same.",
    "    A broken guard and an absent guard look identical from outside, which",
    "    is why tests/test_o_claude_guard.sh runs the script against synthetic",
    "    payloads instead of reading it. Run ./scripts/test.sh after any edit.",
    "  · THE GUARD NEVER ANSWERS permissionDecision 'allow'. Claude Code",
    "    accepts it, and it is an ELEVATION: it approves the call and skips the",
    "    permission prompt that otherwise guards your interactive session. The",
    "    guard's pass is the empty document '{}', which leaves the normal",
    "    permission flow exactly as it was. 'ask' is unused too — an",
    "    unattended cron run has nobody to ask, so 'ask' there is a hang.",
    "",
    "autoMemoryDirectory: where this CLI keeps its own memory. Read AGENTS.md",
    "on what that memory is allowed to be: a CACHE. The single source of truth",
    "is the plain files (ssot/, judgment/, approval_queue.md, verifiers.md,",
    "system_map.md, projects/*/charter.md) and nothing else. Delete the memory",
    "directory and the loop must still be correct — only slower.",
    "Replace <ABSOLUTE-PATH-TO-YOUR-WORK-LOOP> below, or drop the key entirely",
    "to use the CLI's default location."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "date '+[now] %Y-%m-%d (%a) %H:%M %Z'"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__.*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/outbound_guard.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "autoMemoryDirectory": "<ABSOLUTE-PATH-TO-YOUR-WORK-LOOP>/local/memory"
}
